From 0a6329fb45e5576cfd322c75a19b5c94f4447f60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 22:38:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10205/11362] Repair 37 malformed inference_substrate
 declarations (class a of the ARC lint debt)

MEASURED FIRST, per the 2026-08-29 known-issues entry. Re-derived with the
lint's own selector before any write: 573 ARC candidates, 444 failing, 194
INVALID_INFERENCE_SUBSTRATE. Of the 194, THIRTY-EIGHT are the malformed
class: a LEGAL substrate name followed by a trailing human note (space,
';', or '(' separator). The known-issues entry estimated ~23; the
re-derived count is 38 (32 verifier_ensemble_against_cached_candidates,
5 aggregation_from_upstream_artifacts, 1 live_llm_inference).

THE CONVENTION CONFLICT IS THE ROOT CAUSE, and it is a finding on its own:
scripts/determination_preservation_lint.py documents
'<canonical value><separator><human note>' as the project's convention
(233+ live declarations) and its Rule-4 matcher deliberately strips the
note; scripts/arc_artifact_lint.py exact-matches and INVALIDs the same
form. Two guards encode contradictory conventions. This commit repairs
the artifacts to the form BOTH guards accept: the bare canonical value,
with the trailing note moved verbatim to
inference_substrate_original_invalid_value plus a dated
inference_substrate_correction_note (the exp3946 corrigendum pattern).

Append-only: no field deleted, no measurement touched, substrate MEANING
unchanged in every file (the canonical head token is identical before and
after; Rule 4 note-stripping already read these as the same value).

37 of the 38 are repaired here. The 38th,
experiment_4752_held_out_first_win_readiness.json, is deliberately NOT
repaired: its declaration reads 'live_llm_inference -- ... 60s floor
unless a lever-cache hit aggregates an existing proxy artifact', and its
duration_s is 11.3s -- below the 60s live floor, consistent with the
lever-cache branch having actually run. Which substrate truly ran needs a
judgement about the run, not a formatting repair, so it is reported
rather than guessed.

Residual, disclosed: experiment_4751_levelup_selfplay.json now passes the
substrate check but still fails DURATION_MISSING -- duration_s is
genuinely absent and is NOT fabricated here. That is a separate,
pre-existing defect now visible instead of masked by the INVALID error.

Verified: all 37 parse, all declare an exactly-legal substrate, 35/37 are
fully lint-clean (exp4751 above; all others CLEAN),
determination-preservation-lint OK on the staged set.

